    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12052" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">curvāmen</span></b> , ĭnis,
			n.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				bending, bend, vaulting</i> (not ante-Aug.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perh. first used by Ov.): patriae curvamina
					ripae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					9, 450</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 130</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 672</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haec (villa) unum sinum molli curvamine
					amplectitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 9, 7, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caeli,</span>”
				<i>of the climate</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 14, 1, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
